# starformation_and_feedback with R3's flags (FIREmodeOn 1, SFprescription 1,
# BulgeSizeOn 3) at substep 0 on a stable disk: the satellite's Vvir 300 km/s with params.ZZ[31] = 5.122880326409248, a constructed
# redshift found by a scan of the doubles near the analytic root so that eta_raw equals eta_max
# exactly: the strict comparison (X:149) returns eta_raw, the same value.
# Galaxies 0 (the FoF central) and 1 (the forming satellite, p) start from the R3 reference
# group at Snap_32 (rows 4 and 5 of /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R3/model_0.hdf5,
# SHA-256 ab278992616f7137b526e5bd3a43045f2e753e29d84997fc69350255c38f570c); the fields this comment names are
# constructed, every other field is the row's end-of-snapshot value (OutflowRate
# 0 unless named, zero histories, MassLoading the row's stale value).
# Reachability: constructed routine-domain probe
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine starformation_and_feedback_fire

